===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰrewh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|bred}}, {{m|enm|breed}}, from {{inh|en|ang|brēad||fragment, bit, morsel, crumb", also "bread}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*braud}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*braudą||cooked food, leavened bread}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰerw-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*bʰrew-||to boil, seethe}} (see {{doublet|notext=1|en|brew}}). Alternatively, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*braudaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*brauþaz||broken piece, fragment}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰera-||to split, beat, hew, struggle}} (see {{l|en|brittle}}). Perhaps a conflation of the two. Possibly a {{doublet|en|broa|nocap=1}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|breid||bread}}, {{cog|stq|Brad||bread}}, {{cog|fy|brea||bread}}, {{cog|nl|brood||bread}}, {{cog|de|Brot||bread}}, {{cog|da|-}} and {{cog|no|brød||bread}}, {{cog|sv|bröd||bread}}, {{cog|is|brauð||bread}}, {{cog|sq|brydh||I make crumbly, friable, soft}}, {{cog|la|frustum||crumb}}. Eclipsed non-native {{noncog|enm|payn|t=bread}}, borrowed from {{noncog|fro|pain|t=bread}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}}
## {{senseid|en|Q7802}}A [[foodstuff]] made by [[bake|baking]] [[dough]] made from [[cereal]]s.
##: {{ux|en|We made sandwiches with the '''bread''' we bought from the bakery.}}
##: {{ux|en|Any leftover '''bread''' can be put into the pudding.}}
##* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=8|passage=Philander went into the next room{{...}}and came back with a salt mackerel that dripped brine like a rainstorm. Then he put the coffee pot on the stove and rummaged out a loaf of dry '''bread''' and some hardtack.}}
## Food; sustenance; support of life, in general.
##: {{syn|en|staff of life}}
##* {{RQ:KJV|Matthew|4|11||Give us this day our daily '''bread'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any variety of bread.
#: {{ux|en|Some '''breads''' are harder than others.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|US|or|Cockney}} [[money|Money]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:money}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1962|year_published=1963|month_published=January|author=w:James Baldwin|title={{w|Another Country (novel)|Another Country}}|location=New York, N. Y.|publisher=w:The Dial Press|pages=3–4|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/anothercountry0000bald/page/4/mode/2up?q=bread|passage=Maybe somebody would see him and recognize him, maybe one of the guys would lay enough '''bread''' on him for a meal or at least subway fare.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1967|artist=w:Eric Burdon; w:The Animals|album=Winds of Change|title=w:San Franciscan Nights|passage={{...|This is a very personal song, so if the viewer cannot understand it, particularly those of you who are European residents,}} save up all your '''bread''', and fly Trans-Love Airways to San Francisco, USA.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1973|composer=w:Billy Joel|author=w:Billy Joel|artist=w:Billy Joel|title=[[w:Piano Man (song)|Piano Man]]|passage=And they sit at the bar and put '''bread''' in my jar / And say, "Man, what are you doing here?"}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=Jordan Houston; Darnell Carlton; Paul Beauregard; Premro Smith; Marlon Goodwin; David Brown; Willie Hutchinson|passage=Tastes like fruit when you hit it; got to have '''bread''' to get it.|url=https://genius.com/Three-6-mafia-stay-fly-lyrics|title=Stay Fly|publisher=Sony BMG|year=2005|album=Most Known Unknown|artist=Three 6 Mafia (featuring Young Buck, 8 Ball, and MJG)}}

